# Trivy CVE allowlist for dravr-platform image scans.
#
# Each entry MUST include:
#   - the CVE ID alone on a line
#   - a leading comment block explaining: which image, why ignored, when to remove
#
# Entries here suppress Trivy's exit-code 1 in scripts/CI (publish-images.yml)
# while still surfacing the finding in GitHub Code Scanning. Remove an entry as
# soon as the upstream fix lands so the alert closes itself.
#
# Currently empty: the frontend nginx CVEs that lived here (CVE-2026-9256,
# CVE-2026-49975) were patched at the source by switching the frontend runtime
# from the official nginx:alpine image (nginx.org's unpatched r1) to alpine's own
# patched nginx — see docker/images/frontend/Dockerfile. No active allowlist needed.

# sciotte + server images: adm-zip 0.5.17 (HIGH, CVE-2026-39244) is vendored
# inside the GitHub Copilot CLI npm package, which is deliberately pinned at
# 1.0.59 (newer CLIs regress the MCP bridge — see memory/copilot CLI
# regression). Not reachable from the scrape/login path; the CLI only spawns
# for vision-login LLM calls. Remove when the CLI pin can advance to a version
# bundling adm-zip >= 0.6.0.
CVE-2026-39244
